{
  "key": "pr-303",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "fix(cli): FileSystemException handler reports the file path",
    "description": "## Problem

`dmtools run` on a failing factory leg printed exactly one line: `Error: Cannot open file` (live: run 36614989141 — pr-301 review died like that for hours, undiagnosable). The `on FileSystemException` handler in [CliDispatcher] printed only `e.message` — for a failed `File.open` that message is literally "Cannot open file"; the path lives in `e.path` and was discarded.

## Fix

- Include `e.path` and `e.osError?.message` in the handler output.
- Regression test: an unreadable (chmod 000) config must produce an error line containing the path.

## Why it matters

The dmtools-dart factory legs die at this exact spot; with the path visible the next failure names the file instead of hiding it."
  }
}

